**Name aliases**

- **Menace** = **Ace** (short). Same cat. Prefer **Menace** in full roster copy; **Ace** is fine as the short form Ash uses.
- **Mayhem** = **May** = product copy **May Mayhem** (`may-mayhem`). Same cat. Prefer **Mayhem** in full; **May** is fine as the short form Ash uses.
- Spelling: **Jynx** (not Jinx). **Luci** (not Lucy / Lucia / Lucie). **Mayhem** (not Mayham). **Menace** / **Ace**.

Editorial personality **Mr. Murder Mittens** is retired on-site. The knife-toy cat is **Ace / Menace** (`ace-menace`). Do not reintroduce Murder Mittens as a real or editorial sixth cat.

## Ace / Menace (confirmed)

- **Names:** Menace (full), Ace (short)
- **Pronouns:** he/him
- **Personality:** Extra lovey and vociferous — affectionate + loud/talky energy (Ash: “voicetrous”)
- **Look:** High-contrast brown/gold tabby with bold black stripes and spots/rosettes (Bengal-leaning look); bright yellow-green eyes; often mid-play with toys
- **Reference photos:**
  - `.cursor/references/cats/ace.jpg` — on his back with the bloody plush chef’s knife
  - `.cursor/references/cats/ace-2.jpg` — upright, biting/holding the bloody knife toy

## May / Mayhem (confirmed)

- **Names:** Mayhem (full), May (short)
- **Pronouns:** she/her
- **Personality:** Naughty — chaos energy; when her name is on a pick, it should match real mischief, not a sticker aesthetic
- **Look:** Lighter / white–cream base with soft grey-tan tabby points (face, ears, legs, striped tail); **bright blue eyes** (strong visual ID vs Jynx, Luci, Ace)
- **Reference photos:**
  - `.cursor/references/cats/may.jpg` — adult May upright with the bloody plush axe toy (pink/blue spiked collar)
  - `.cursor/references/cats/may-luci-kittens.jpg` — kitten pair; **May is the white/blue-eyed one on the left**

